1. THE CURRENTS BY CLASS (each from its pinned source)
   continuous: the pack's declared 10.0 A; the drafted states at the gauge's 10.0 V floor (record l9pwr section 6): the largest
     sustained PLAN 9.63 A (PS-BUSY), at HIGH 14.97 A (PS-BUSY), with the outlets 19.20 A (PS-BUSY plus both outlets); above 10.0 A the shedding control holds a state
   transient: 18.0 A for at most 60 s (PWR-F12, every transmitter; ended early above 18.0 A by firmware), judged as if steady; the
     largest key-down row 21.93 A at PLAN at 10.0 V (PS-ALLTX); the PA's key-on step 6.4 to 9.6 A; the docking pulse 242.9 A peak, 33.8 us
     time constant, I2t 0.9971 A2s, once per docking (L4-E11 E11-30)
   fault, the gauge working (the image): OCD1 20.0 A, 2 s; OCD2 24.0 A, 1 s; AOLD 30.0 A, 0.02 s; ASCD 55.6 A, 244 us
     so 20.0 A may be held with no trip; every level is firmware-configured (W4DP-F2)
   fault, board P's FETs failed short: the 25 A MINI blades read monotone (Littelfuse 297): up to 135 %, no opening assured; 135 to 200 %, at most 600 s; 200 to 350 %, at most 5 s; 350 to 600 %, at most 0.5 s; over 600 % to 480 A, at most 0.1 s
     nominal melting I2t 625 A2s (no clearing I2t printed); F2 (Eaton SCF9550, 30 A) 100 % for 1 h minimum, 200 % within 60 s
     the cells' continuous rating at 3P: 24 A (pcb_pack_protection.yaml); prospective fault 240 to 480 A
   the shore input: 6.15 A continuous; F1 10 A MINI read monotone: up to 135 %, no opening assured; 135 to 200 %, at most 600 s; 200 to 350 %, at most 5 s; 350 to 600 %, at most 0.5 s; over 600 % to 900 A, at most 0.1 s
     (L4-E11 section 6); its D-06 selection: board E's copper from J_DCIN to F1 to the clamps at least 20 A continuous
   VIN_RAW: declared 14.10 A; the tracker's minimum valley limit 13.8 A; with the hot-swap 19.95 A until its fault time
   the inside air: the consolidation's +70 C line (with the hold); L4-E12's E3-O 71.25 C and E5's dwell 76.25 C (steady, without the
     hold): every final temperature below starts from 76.25 C

2. THE METHOD (decision 35's model, applied to the copper as it is stacked)
   rating: track_current.conservative at each area, outer copper at EXTERNAL_FACTOR 2.0 once; widths track_current.width_for_current
     at its 10 K default; the fits' data: IPC-2152 to 30 A and 100 K, CNES to 8 A (ECSS-Q-ST-70-12C D.2, D.3)
   the two outer faces of a band share one footprint and its two cooling surfaces, so they are ONE conductor of their combined
     section (a 1 oz pair is a 2 oz conductor of the band's width); a band and its return run side by side at both connector ends,
     so the pair is ONE conductor of twice the width and both faces' copper carrying their combined dissipation (the current sqrt(2 (kf^2 + kr^2)) x I)
     and its width per band per face is half of width_for_current at that current and twice the face weight; no credit is held for
     laying the return apart, so the widths 'apart' are printed for comparison only
   an uneven split s between the faces dissipates k^2 = 2 (s^2 + (1 - s)^2) of an even one: 1.0100 at s 0.55
   before a timed clearance: the smaller of the steady rise and the governing face's adiabatic rise (Onderdonk, constants 234 and
     33, copper melting 1083 C, as records/l7pwr/inputs holds it); a constant current never passes its steady rise
   the limit of a band: the lowest printed limit of the parts it joins (the laminate's is NOT HELD):
     pack A   105 C, the blade (MINI 297) (the blade (MINI 297) 105 C; the 3568 holder 145 C); with the blade's plating pinned 125 C
     pack E   105 C, the blade (MINI 297) (the blade (MINI 297) 105 C; the 3568 holder 145 C; the XT60 120 C); with the blade's plating pinned 120 C
     shore E  105 C, the blade (MINI, 10 A; the 297's figures, the 997's not held) (the blade (MINI, 10 A; the 297's figures, the 997's not held) 105 C; the 3568 holder 145 C; J_DCIN (JST VH, as drawn) 105 C); with the blade's plating pinned 105 C
     the blade: fitted as Keystone 3568 (holder); Littelfuse 0297025 MINI 297 25 A (fuse, fitted at build); silver terminals 125 C, tin 105 C; the MPN that pins silver: 0297025.WXNV (tin: 0297025.WXT)
     the parts with no printed limit held: R17 (ROHM GMR100HJAAFD5L00), R19 (HoJLR2512-3W-10mR-1%), the Mill-Max pins' range (unreadable in the filed page)
   criteria (SESSION): the continuous load, the transient, every gauge level and the 25 A case within the ruled 10 K; every
     backstop interval and short at or under the band's limit from 76.25 C; every part against its printed rating

3. THE SPLIT, THE TRANSFER FIELDS AND THE BARRELS
   through-hole at both ends: equal faces share evenly; a one-face part at one end: the part's face carries (Rb + Rv) / (2 Rb + Rv);
     at both ends (Rb + 2 Rv) / (2 Rb + 2 Rv); stitching along such a band moves current onto the part's face early, so the transfer
     barrels sit in a field at the part. With the faces as one conductor the split matters through its dissipation: one barrel of
     0.0236 mm2 is worth 91.9 mm of a 39.14 mm band, and with one barrel the part's face carries 0.95 at 5 mm, 0.91 at 10 mm, 0.85 at 20 mm, 0.77 at 40 mm, 0.68 at 80 mm (k 1.347, 1.294, 1.219, 1.134, 1.065)
   the barrel's annulus, two conventions (via_current's 18 um average plating):
     outward  0.02364 mm2, 0.900 A at 10 K; thermal counts at half the coordination current: pack 14, shore 12, VIN_RAW 8
     inward   0.02160 mm2, 0.843 A at 10 K; thermal counts at half the coordination current: pack 15, shore 12, VIN_RAW 9
     (outward: the 0.4 mm is the finished hole and the plating lies outside it, via_current's pi (d + t) t; inward: the 0.4 mm is the
     drill and the plating lies inside, pi (d - t) t; the field takes the inward count until the fabricator states which)
   the field at each one-face end: the inward count at 10 K (pack 15, shore 12) or the count that holds the blade's 600 s point within
     the band's limit (pack: every interval to the blade's 600 s point, 16; shore: every interval to F1's 0.5 s one, 15), whichever
     is more: pack 16, shore 15; and the split count below where it is more
   the split count each one-face end needs for the part's face to carry at most 0.55 (one end / both ends):
     pack, board A, 1 oz    39.14 mm, 1.5384 mm board: 5 mm 81 / 161, 10 mm 41 / 81, 20 mm 21 / 41, 40 mm 11 / 21, 80 mm 6 / 11
     pack, board E, 1 oz    39.14 mm, 1.5862 mm board: 5 mm 83 / 166, 10 mm 42 / 83, 20 mm 21 / 42, 40 mm 11 / 21, 80 mm 6 / 11
     pack, board E, 2 oz    19.57 mm, 1.5862 mm board: 5 mm 83 / 166, 10 mm 42 / 83, 20 mm 21 / 42, 40 mm 11 / 21, 80 mm 6 / 11
     shore, board E, 1 oz   26.02 mm, 1.5862 mm board: 5 mm 55 / 110, 10 mm 28 / 55, 20 mm 14 / 28, 40 mm 7 / 14, 80 mm 4 / 7

